{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 10, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III was the Count of Tripoli from 1152 to 1152 and a member of the Anjou dynasty He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Ermengarde of Alpilles \n\n*Early Life and Accession*\n\nRaymond III was born in 1127 and succeeded his father as Count of Tripoli at the age of 25 In 1148 he married Eschiva of Alpilles a member of the Alpilles family \n\nThe marriage between Raymond and Eschiva was a strategic one aimed at strengthening the ties between the Anjou dynasty and the Alpilles family \n\nRaymond III ruled over the Kingdom of Tripoli for nearly two years until his death in 1152 \n\n*Reign*\n\nDuring his reign Raymond III focused on consolidating his power and securing the borders of the kingdom \n\nHe launched a series of military campaigns against the Zengid dynasty which controlled much of the Middle East \n\nRaymond's military campaigns were largely unsuccessful and he was eventually forced to negotiate a peace treaty with the Zengids \n\nDespite his military failures Raymond III was able to maintain control over the Kingdom of Tripoli and secure its borders \n\n*Death and Succession*\n\nRaymond III died in 1152 at the age of 25 without any surviving children \n\nHis death led to a succession crisis in the Kingdom of Tripoli \n\nThe throne was eventually claimed by Bohemond III Count of Tripoli who was a member of the Anjou dynasty \n\nBohemond III would go on to rule the Kingdom of Tripoli for the next several decades and secure its position as a major power in the Middle East", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.001581966644152999}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0001299296854995191}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -1.9862117767333984}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.4664328396320343}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.7896010279655457}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -8.3